{"id": "unknown-2026-11-13-011", "date": "2026-11-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["ramp up"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Sodium-ion batteries close gap with lithium-ion as utility-scale storage opportunities grow", "content": "<p>Sodium-ion batteries are approaching lithium-ion performance in key areas, with commercial cells reaching energy densities of 175 Wh/kg and offering strong low-temperature performance. Silvia Bodoardo, professor at the Polytechnic University of Turin, told <b>pv magazine</b> that utility-scale energy storage represents the technology’s most promising market, as manufacturers ramp up production.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/13/sodium-ion-batteries-close-gap-with", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/13/sodium-ion-batteries-close-gap-with-lithium-ion-as-utility-scale-storage-opportunities-grow/", "type": "rss"}]}
